An index renamed, its definition the same: the old one dropped, the new
one made. The table is not touched.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE INDEX dish_name ON dish (name);
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE INDEX dish_by_name ON dish (name);

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 2 steps
  index `dish_name`: not in schema.sql
    DROP INDEX "dish_name"
  index `dish_by_name`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE INDEX dish_by_name ON dish (name)
